------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Flag of Kuala Lumpur (skylineqr-core/.../city/Vehicles.kt)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The banner the plane tows is drawn after "Flag of Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia.svg"
on Wikimedia Commons
(https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Kuala_Lumpur,_Malaysia.svg),
which is in the public domain. Only its proportions and colours are used; no
file from it is included.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Loading poster (map data)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The map poster of Kuala Lumpur shown while the city loads
(skylineqr-web/src/wasmJsMain/resources/kl-poster.webp and
app/src/main/res/drawable-nodpi/kl_poster.webp) was made with maptoposter by
Ankur Gupta (https://github.com/originalankur/maptoposter, MIT License,
Copyright (c) 2026 Ankur Gupta), run unchanged by tools/poster/make_poster.sh;
none of its code is included here. It sets its text in Roboto (Apache License
2.0). The map data is © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the Open
Database License (https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright); the poster prints
that credit on itself.

------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Tap to share (skylineqr-nfc)
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

skylineqr-nfc is written from the public specifications its sources name: NFC
Forum NDEF 1.0 and its URI, Text and Smart Poster record types, Type 2 and
Type 4 Tag 2.0, ISO 7816-4, Wi-Fi Simple Configuration 2.0, vCard 3.0 (RFC
2426) and MECARD. How Tap Tap Tap (com.thangman22.taptaptap) behaves was looked
at; none of its code is used. Its QR scanner uses Google's ML Kit barcode
scanning with the bundled model, under the ML Kit Terms of Service
(https://developers.google.com/ml-kit/terms).

